<!--
  TAOM career-archetype starting equipment rosters (#629).

  Roster ID convention: player_career_{cultureId}_{archetype}_{f|m}
  Applied at the end of character creation by CareerStartingEquipmentService through
  Equipment.FillFrom, which copies all 12 slots (Equipment.cs:184-194): this is the WHOLE
  battle set, not a merge over the culture default. Head, Cape and Gloves are empty by design.
  The civilian set still comes from the culture-default roster for the youth title.

  Archetypes (CareerArchetype.cs):
    ranged   - bow + arrows + one-handed sidearm
    cavalry  - polearm + shield + sidearm + horse + harness
    infantry - one-handed weapon + shield + polearm (Dol Guldur: two-handed axe)

  The five weapon and armour slots are GENERATED by tools/generate_career_kits.py, whose verify
  mode pins them: each is gear the culture's own troops carry, taken from its lowest tiers.
  Per slot: the lowest-level item of that class a non-hero troop of the culture carries in a
  battle set, preferring a non-vanilla item first carried at level 21 or below, otherwise the
  lowest troop's own item even when vanilla; a bow first takes the lowest Bow skill requirement,
  so a new character can re-equip it. Erebor and Dunland carry a one-handed axe as the sidearm.
  The non-vanilla preference lifts a few picks above the culture's very lowest troop (issue #629
  lists them). StarterKitCoverageTests pins that a troop of the culture carries every item.
  Horse and HorseHarness are hand-kept: the Armory has no riding horse of its own.

  taom_player_start_vanilla_override.xml is GENERATED from this file by
  tools/wire_starter_kit_rosters.py; re-run it after any change here.
  Lothlorien, Umbar and Khand (battania) have no career rosters and fall through to the
  culture-default roster via ICareerStartingEquipmentService graceful fallback.
-->
